#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""penultimate - a tile-based fantasy role-playing game in Python + Tk.

Standard library only.  In the spirit of Ultima I-IV: one adventurer wanders
an overworld of towns, dungeons and wilderness, talks to townsfolk, buys
weapons and armour, and runs errands for Lord Canadian, the kindly (and
endlessly apologetic) ruler of the realm.  Moosedain the Wicked has sent his
minions to steal four royal relics; recover them, and Lord Canadian will
forge the Maple Blade, the one weapon that can harm Moosedain himself.

Every new game generates a new world (map, towns, people, dungeons, quests);
within a game the world is fixed.  The game is saved to ~/.penultimate.json
whenever you change location and when you quit, and resumed next time.

Talking: walk into a person (or into a shop counter with someone behind it),
then type a word and press Return.  Everyone knows NAME, JOB and BYE; most
people know NEWS, and words in CAPITALS are worth asking about.  Shopkeepers
answer BUY.  Lord Canadian heals you and raises your level when you have
earned it.  Dying is not the end: Lord Canadian resurrects you, but your gold
is lost.

Keys:  arrows / WASD   move (into monsters to fight, into people to talk)
       space           wait a turn        P   drink a healing potion
       M               map                ?   help
       + / -           zoom in / out      V   sound effects on / off
       B               music on / off
       N               new game           Ctrl-Q / Cmd-Q   quit

Sound effects and chiptune music (a tune each for the wilderness, towns,
the castle and dungeons) are synthesized and played with afplay (macOS),
paplay or aplay if one is available; otherwise the game is silent.  The
music is rendered once and cached in ~/.cache/penultimate.

App bundle (macOS):  penultimate --build-app [DIR]   builds penultimate.app
                     penultimate --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

The tile graphics are PNGs stored in this file (TILE_PNG); their pixel-art
source is make_tiles.py, which regenerates that block.
"""

